Ex. No.: 01              ARRAY OPERATIONS 
Date:  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

Aim 
To perform basic array operations (Display, Insert, Delete, and Modify). 
Procedure 
1. Start the program.  
2. Read the array elements.  
3. Display the original array.  
4. Add a new element at the end of the array.  
5. Remove the last element from the array.  
6. Change the value of an existing element.  
7. Display the updated array and stop.  

Program 
#include <stdio.h> 
int main() 
{ 
    int a[10], n, i; 
 
    printf("Enter number of elements: "); 
    scanf("%d", &n); 
 
    printf("Enter array elements:\n"); 
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++) 
    { 
        scanf("%d", &a[i]); 
    } 
 
    printf("\nOriginal Array: "); 
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", a[i]); 
    } 
 
    a[n] = 60; /* Insert Operation */ 
    n++; 
 
    printf("\nAfter Insertion: "); 
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", a[i]); 
    } 
 
       n--;  /* Delete Operation */ 
 
    printf("\nAfter Deletion: "); 
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", a[i]); 
    } 
 
    a[1] = 99;     /* Modify Operation */ 
 
    printf("\nAfter Modification: "); 
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++) 
    { 
        printf("%d ", a[i]); 
    } 
 
    return 0; 
} 
 
Output 
Enter number of elements: 5 
Enter array elements: 
10 20 30 40 50 
 
Original Array: 10 20 30 40 50 
After Insertion: 10 20 30 40 50 60 
After Deletion: 10 20 30 40 50 
After Modification: 10 99 30 40 50 
 
Result 
Thus, the basic array operations such as insertion, deletion, and modification were performed 
successfully using C programming.
